        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: Mining is done underground, followed by beneficiation trough flotation where considerable amounts of agents and lime are added. Overburden and tailings are disposed on the mining site and partly re-filled. This module covers the five major production routes, aggregated according to their market share in 1994. Sulphur dioxide in the off-gas is recovered producing sulphuric acid. For electricity mix a mix of 60% hydropower and 40% electricity at grid was chosen.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
